TYPES.md §9.3, EVALUATION.md §8.1, log-2026-11-01 "EVAL-OWED review FAIL", "NOTENTRY report": lr is
reached first as itself, no entry, then as kl's entry y. The check reading self.id is E4003 on lr, and
gets its normal verdict at kl[y]: false, E5001. On ta's entry it holds.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// A row.
record Row {
  /// Its code.
  code: String

  check notY: self.id != "y" else "id y"
}

/// The rows.
let ta: table Row = { a { code: "a" } }

/// A row that is no entry.
let lr: Row = { code: "y" }

/// Keyed by code, holding lr.
let kl: [Row] keyed by code = [lr]
-- findings.txt --
error[E4003]  a/a.canon:9:15
  lr: .id of a value that is not an entry of a table or keyed list

error[E5001]  a/a.canon:16:15
  kl[y]: id y
  expected by a/a.canon:9 (check notY)

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
